          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system"}> orthogonal
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system"} factorization system
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            consists of two classes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,M)
            such that every morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            factors as an
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "-morphism," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
            –uniquely for the orthogonal case,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\perp m
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonality"} orthogonality
            – for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\in E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
            \.
          %p
            To
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enrich
            this, we should first consider enriched orthogonality. The statement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\perp m
            for maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:A\to B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:X\to Y
            can be rephrased by saying that the square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi B
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi B
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{C(B,X) &amp; \to &amp; C(A,X)\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                  C(B,Y) &amp; \to &amp; C(A,Y)}
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p More generally, the statement that there exists at least one lift is to say that the canonical morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C(B,X) \to C(A,X) \prod_{C(A,Y)} C(B,Y)
          %p
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} split epimorphism
          %p
            It is then clear that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is enriched over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\perp m
            in an enriched sense, we should instead require this square to be a pullback of enriched
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            are still maps in the underlying ordinary category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
          %p
            Therefore, we define an
            %strong enriched (orthogonal) factorization system
            on an enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to consist of two classes of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,M)
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            such that
          %ol
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\perp m
              in the above enriched sense for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\in E
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
            %li
              Every map in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
              factors as an
              = succeed "-map" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              = succeed "-map." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %p
            By the definition of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            induces an ordinary factorization system on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} power
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            implies enriched orthogonality by a Yoneda lemma argument.
          %h2#functoriality Functoriality
          %p
            Moreover, the factorization functor can be made into an enriched functor in the following way. There is a
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{2}}
            whose objects are morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            and whose hom-objects are defined by, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1:X_1\to Y_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_2:X_2\to Y_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{C^{\mathbf{2}}(f_1,f_2) &amp; \to &amp; C(X_1,X_2)\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                  C(Y_1,Y_2) &amp; \to &amp; C(X_1,Y_2).}
          %p
            (This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} power
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\mathbf{2}}
            in the 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V-Cat
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [{\mathbf{2}}_V,C]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\mathbf{2}}_V
            denotes the free
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\mathbf{2}}
          %p
            Likewise, we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{3}}
            whose objects are composable pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi Y
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\overset{f}{\to} Y \overset{g}{\to} Z
            of morphisms in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{C^{\mathbf{3}}((f_1,g_1),(f_2,g_2)) &amp; \to &amp; C^{\mathbf{2}}(f_1,f_2)\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                  C^{\mathbf{2}}(g_1,g_2) &amp; \to &amp; C(Y_1,Y_2).}
          %p
            By functoriality we then mean that the factorization is given by a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{2}} \to C^{\mathbf{3}}
            which, when composed with the “composition” functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{3}} \to C^{\mathbf{2}}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{2}}
          %p
            The interesting part of the enrichment of this functor is the following: given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1:X_1\to Z_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_2:X_2\to Z_2
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{2}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \overset{m_1}{\to} Y_1 \overset{e_1}{\to} Z_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi m
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2 \overset{m_2}{\to} Y_2 \overset{e_2}{\to} Z_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi Z
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi Z
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{C(Y_1,Y_2) &amp; \to &amp; C(X_1,Y_2)\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow\\
                  C(Y_1,Z_2) &amp; \to &amp; C(X_1,Z_2)}
          %p and we also have a commutative square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 2
